<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.17.3: Changing the Parameters of a Quadratic Expression</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02049</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.17.3: Changing the Parameters of a Quadratic Expression</md:title>
    <md:uuid>287c0fd8-c87f-45a6-941b-47bfe6dd8c2a</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>Mai is learning to create computer animation by programming. In one part of her animation, she uses a quadratic function to model the path of the main character, an animated peanut, jumping over a wall.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/0250370ba6ce91f28fddd3ccbf84c786f82ea604"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Mai uses the equation \(y=-0.1(x−h)^2+k\) to represent the path of the jump. \(y\) represents the height of the peanut as a function of the horizontal distance it travels, \(x\).</para>
<para>On the screen, the base of the wall is located at \((22,0)\), with the top of the wall at \((22,4.5)\). The dashed curve in the picture shows the graph of one equation Mai tried, where the peanut fails to make it over the wall.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/312cbbfe4c145142e6004586cfa01b526d2431a1"/></media></figure></para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="9086e747-829f-4fe5-b52e-3c3ddd4ed20e" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="74f38a7a-47eb-4bab-be6b-21e6789ce1b2" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="18">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the value of \(h\) in this equation?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here: </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="ba52707a-d0ea-4e23-8dca-a6370289ad30" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="5">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the value of \(k\) in this equation?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here: </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
